# Billing — Dev provider simulate (non-production only)
# UC-138: fire one provider event at the fake billing provider. Registered only when APP_ENV is local
# or staging (404 in production), behind both operator keys. It works only for a charge whose
# merchant profile is a *_FAKE key, and the fake keeps its charges in memory: after a backend restart
# (or on a second instance) the request is a 409 until a new charge exists.
#
# Exactly one of tenantId / chargeId. With tenantId the charge is the tenant's single open charge
# (PAID_*, OVERDUE) or its most recent paid charge (REFUND_*, CHARGEBACK_*).
#
# Prerequisites:
#   1. pnpm infra:up
#   2. pnpm --filter @ikaro/backend run dev
#   3. a tenant with a charge at the fake provider (provision one, then POST /cron/billing-issue-charges)
#
# REST Client environment: select "local" in VS Code status bar

@baseUrl     = {{backendUrl}}
@internalKey = {{$dotenv INTERNAL_API_KEY}}
@platformKey = {{$dotenv PLATFORM_ADMIN_KEY}}
@tenantId    = REPLACE-WITH-TENANT-UUID
@chargeId    = REPLACE-WITH-CHARGE-UUID

### Pay the tenant's open charge by Pix
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/dev/billing/provider/simulate
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
X-Platform-Admin-Key: {{platformKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenantId": "{{tenantId}}", "event": "PAID_PIX" }

###

### Boleto paid, delivered twice (the second is a recognised duplicate)
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/dev/billing/provider/simulate
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
X-Platform-Admin-Key: {{platformKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "chargeId": "{{chargeId}}", "event": "PAID_BOLETO", "delivery": "DUPLICATE" }

###

### Boleto paid, RECEIVED delivered before CONFIRMED
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/dev/billing/provider/simulate
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
X-Platform-Admin-Key: {{platformKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "chargeId": "{{chargeId}}", "event": "PAID_BOLETO", "delivery": "OUT_OF_ORDER" }

###

### Card paid, delivered after a short in-request wait
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/dev/billing/provider/simulate
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
X-Platform-Admin-Key: {{platformKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "chargeId": "{{chargeId}}", "event": "PAID_CARD", "delivery": "DELAYED" }

###

### Overdue (confirm-only: the status sweep, not the webhook, moves the subscription to PAST_DUE)
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/dev/billing/provider/simulate
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
X-Platform-Admin-Key: {{platformKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenantId": "{{tenantId}}", "event": "OVERDUE" }

###

### Refund the tenant's most recent paid charge
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/dev/billing/provider/simulate
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
X-Platform-Admin-Key: {{platformKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenantId": "{{tenantId}}", "event": "REFUND_FULL" }

###

### Dispute opened, then lost
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/dev/billing/provider/simulate
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
X-Platform-Admin-Key: {{platformKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenantId": "{{tenantId}}", "event": "CHARGEBACK_OPENED" }

###

POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/dev/billing/provider/simulate
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
X-Platform-Admin-Key: {{platformKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenantId": "{{tenantId}}", "event": "CHARGEBACK_LOST" }

###

### The next provider call fails once (here the webhook's re-read), so the payment is not applied
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/dev/billing/provider/simulate
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
X-Platform-Admin-Key: {{platformKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenantId": "{{tenantId}}", "event": "PAID_PIX", "failure": "PROVIDER_5XX" }

###

### Invalid: both ids → 400; an event that does not apply or an unknown charge → 409
POST {{baseUrl}}/internal/dev/billing/provider/simulate
X-Internal-Key: {{internalKey}}
X-Platform-Admin-Key: {{platformKey}}
Content-Type: application/json

{ "tenantId": "{{tenantId}}", "chargeId": "{{chargeId}}", "event": "PAID_PIX" }
